if i give the card details.. is that take money automatically?
Yes, adding a credit or debit card typically sets your account to automatic billing, which means you will be charged automatically as you run ads. We charge your card whenever your ad costs reach a specific amount called a payment threshold, and again on your monthly bill date for any remaining costs.
How Automatic Billing Works
Payment Threshold: This is a set amount of spend that triggers a charge. When you first start, this threshold is small (e.g., ₹500) and increases as you make successful payments.
Monthly Bill Date: If you have any unpaid costs at the end of your billing cycle that haven't reached your threshold, you'll be charged for that remaining balance once a month.
RBI Regulations in India: Since your account is based in India, automatic payments are subject to eMandate regulations from the Reserve Bank of India (RBI). This may affect how recurring payments are processed on your card.
If you prefer to control exactly when money is taken, you can also use available funds (prepaid) by adding money to your account in advance using methods like UPI or Net Banking. In that case, we deduct from your balance daily as your ads run.
