what is the charge for sending message to customer?
WhatsApp Business Platform charges are based on the category of the message and the recipient's country. You are only charged when a message is successfully delivered.
Message Categories and Pricing
Marketing messages: Used for promotions, awareness, or driving sales. These typically have the highest rates.
Utility messages: Used for specific customer requests or transactions, like order confirmations or fraud alerts.
Authentication messages: Used to verify a customer's identity with one-time passcodes (OTPs).
Service messages: These are free-form replies to customer-initiated messages. You are not charged for these if they are sent within a 24-hour customer service window.
Free Message Opportunities
Service & Utility Replies: All service and utility messages sent in response to customers within the 24-hour window are free.
Free Entry Point Window: If a customer messages you from a Facebook or Instagram ad that clicks to WhatsApp, you get a 72-hour window where all messages to that customer are free.
For the exact costs in your region, you can view the WhatsApp Business Platform rate cards.
